l_nonzero_rc_returns_empty_dict():\n    module = FakeModule(run_command_result=(1, 'ignored', 'some error'))\n    result = get_sysctl(module, ['-a'])\n\n    assert result == {}\n    assert module.warnings == []\n\n\ndef test_get_sysctl_empty_output_returns_empty_dict():\n    module = FakeModule(run_command_result=(0, '', ''))\n    result = get_sysctl(module, [])\n\n    assert result == {}\n    assert module.warnings == []\n\n\ndef test_get_sysctl_run_command_oserror_warns_and_returns_empty_dict():\n    module = FakeModule(run_command_exc=OSError(2, 'No such file or directory'))\n    result = get_sysctl(module, ['-a'])\n\n    assert result == {}\n    assert len(module.warnings) == 1\n    assert 'Unable to read sysctl' in module.warnings[0]\n    assert 'No such file or directory' in module.warnings[0]\n\n\ndef test_get_sysctl_run_command_ioerror_warns_and_returns_empty_dict():\n    module = FakeModule(run_command_exc=IOError('broken pipe'))\n    result = get_sysctl(module, ['-a'])\n\n    assert result == {}\n    assert len(module.warnings) == 1\n    assert 'Unable to read sysctl' in module.warnings[0]\n    assert 'broken pipe' in module.warnings[0]\n```\n\nWait \u2014 in test_get_sysctl_unsplittable_first_line_yields_empty_dict, let me trace: out = 'noseparator\\n'. splitlines \u2192 ['noseparator'].\n- 'noseparator' \u2192 not empty, not starting with ' ', key='' \u2192 no store. re.split fails \u2192 warn. key stays ''.\n- End: key '' \u2192 falsy \u2192 no store.\nResult: {}. Good, covers 59 false branch with loop executed.\n\nAnd test_get_sysctl_empty_output covers 59 false with loop not executed. Both fine.\n\nOne more consideration: in the multiline test, the value 'first\\n continued line' \u2014 after strip() it stays the same. But wait, what if the multiline line is the last line? Then at end, key truthy \u2192 sysctl[key] = value.strip(). Covered in basic flow anyway.\n\nAlso, should I test that prefixes are extended correctly with multiple prefixes? test_ge